    87	## B. Theorem B — near-stretched states of any spin f ≥ 2
    88	
    89	Write a highest-weight state of degree v and S_z = fv − k in "deficit" coordinates
    90	z_f^{v−|d|} Π_j z_{f−j}^{d_j}, with Σ_j j d_j = k. Here z_m creates the unnormalized orbital u^{f+m}v^{f−m},
    91	so its Fock weight is w_{f−j} = 1/binom(2f, j). In these coordinates
    92	S₊ z_{f−j} = j z_{f−j+1} does not depend on v or f. For k < 2f the pair operator P lowers the
    93	deficit by 2f, so every such state is harmonic with seniority v. The highest-weight space has
    94	dimension p(k) − p(k−1) (partition numbers): 1 for k = 2 and k = 3. The states are
    95	ψ₂ = z_f^{v−1}z_{f−2} − z_f^{v−2}z_{f−1}² and
    96	ψ₃ = z_f^{v−1}z_{f−3} − 3z_f^{v−2}z_{f−1}z_{f−2} + 2z_f^{v−3}z_{f−1}³.
    97	
    98	**Theorem B.** For every integer spin f ≥ 2 and every v at which both states exist, with parent
    99	spin L = fv − k and daughter spin L' = f(v−1) − k':
   100	
   101	| k → k' | r² | sign |
   102	|---|---|---|
   103	| 2 → 0 | 2(fv−1) / (v(2fv−2f−1)) = 2(L+1)/(v(2L'−1)) | + |
   104	| 2 → 2 | (v−2)(2fv−1) / (v(2fv−2f−1)) = (v−2)(2L+3)/(v(2L'+3)) | + |
   105	| 3 → 0 | f(v−2)(2fv−3) / (v(fv−f−1)(2fv−2f−1)) = f(v−2)(2L+3)/(v(L'−1)(2L'−1)) | − |
   106	| 3 → 2 | 6(f−1)(fv−1) / (v(fv−f−2)(2fv−2f−1)) = 6(f−1)(L+2)/(vL'(2L'+3)) | + |
   107	| 3 → 3 | (v−3)(fv−2)(fv−1) / (v(fv−f−2)(fv−f−1)) = (v−3)(L+1)(L+2)/(v(L'+1)(L'+2)) | + |
   108	
   109	Signs use the phase "coefficient of the largest single deficit positive". With Theorem A, this
   110	gives every one-body CFP of these states for all N and all f, in Bao–Li form.
   111	
   112	*Proof (computer-assisted).* The states ψ₂ and ψ₃ follow from S₊ψ = 0 (shown above). Every CFP is
   113	a finite sum over at most three monomials with Fock weights (v−|d|)! Π d_j! w_{f−j}^{d_j}. The CG
   114	coefficient of the stretched state is ⟨f μ; L' L'|L L⟩² = Π_{i<j}(2L'−i)/(2L+2+i) with
   115	j = f − μ = k − k'. All ratios of factorials have fixed integer offsets, so each r² is an exact
   116	rational function of (v, f). `top_family_symbolic.py general 3` performs this algebra.
   117	
   118	*Hand check of 2 → 0.* X = ⟨ψ₂, z_{f−2}z_f^{v−1}⟩ = (v−1)! w_{f−2}, ‖ψ₂‖² = (v−2)!(2fv−1)/(2f²(2f−1)),
   119	‖z_f^{v−1}‖² = (v−1)!, w_{f−2} = 1/(f(2f−1)) and CG² = (2fv−2f)(2fv−2f−1)/((2fv−2)(2fv−1)).
   120	Then r² = X²/(w_{f−2}‖ψ₂‖²‖φ‖² v CG²) = 2(fv−1)/(v(2fv−2f−1)), as stated.
   121	
   122	*Verification (ran):* `$PY top_family_symbolic.py general 3` printed the table above.
   123	`$PY check_general_f.py` printed `Theorem B formulas agree exactly (with signs) with the
   124	polynomial engine: 200 checks, f = 2..6, v <= 10`. That engine is a separate implementation: full
   125	monomial spaces with a null-space computation.
   126	*Scope:* k = 2, 3 only. For f ≥ 3, k = 4 already has multiplicity 2 (both states have seniority v).
