   128	## C. Spin 2: top families L = 2v − k, k ≤ 8, as rational functions of v
   129	
   130	The deficit method of §B is extended with the harmonic projection
   131	H(φ) = Σ_i β_i (P†)^i P^i φ, β_i = (−1)^i/(2^i i! Π_{l≤i}(D+2v−2−2l)). P acts on the implicit z₂
   132	power through a factor v − |d|. The covariant monomial H^b T^c j^e is fixed in deficit coordinates,
   133	and f^a only fixes the degree. The basis vectors are checked symbolically: S₊ψ = 0 and Pψ = 0
   134	identically in v. Integer roots of the norms, of the CG factors and of the overlaps are checked so
   135	that no excluded v lies in the stated range.
   136	
   137	* **k ≤ 5 (multiplicity-free).** All 14 transitions are products of linear factors, for example
   138	  r²(k=4→4) = (v−4)(2v−3)(2v−1)(4v−5)(4v−3)/(v(2v−5)(2v+1)(4v−9)(4v−7)). The full list is in
   139	  [results/spin2_top_families_k8_asc.txt](results/spin2_top_families_k8_asc.txt). **Reproduction:**
   140	  with τ = v − 1, all 14 nonzero squared entries of Table III of Pan, Bao, Zhang, Draayer (2014)
   141	  are reproduced exactly; signs differ by phase convention.
