   144	  weight into the k' = 2 daughter is Q_{dd} = 3·F(v)/(v(v−2)(2v−5)(2v+1)(4v−11)(4v−9)) with
   145	  F(v) = 32v⁴−288v³+1024v²−1692v+1065. F(τ+1) is exactly Pan et al.'s f(τ+1). Their Table IV
   146	  basis is the **principal-parent basis of the k' = 2 daughter** (χ = 2) and its orthogonal
   147	  complement (χ = 1). All 8 multiplicity-free rows of their Table IV are **reproduced exactly**
