     2	(k = 6, 8, 9, 10, 11; default k = 6, the first multiplicity family).
     3	
     4	For v > k the space V of seniority-v, spin-(2v-k) highest-weight states is 2-dimensional
     5	over K = Q(v), spanned by phi0 = proj(covariant with e = 0) and phi1 = proj(covariant with
     6	e = 1) (for k = 6: f^(v-6) H^3 and f^(v-3) j).  q is the Fock form divided by (v-k)!.
     7	The script prints (exact, symbolic in v):
