    45	
    46	## A. Theorem A — the N-recursion is solved for every spin f
    47	
    48	**Theorem A.** Let N = v + 2n, D = 2f+1, and let |N vαL⟩, |N−1 v'α'L'⟩ be built as in §0
    49	from orthonormal harmonic states. Then c = 0 unless v' = v ± 1, and
    50	
    51	  c(N vαL; N−1, v−1, α'L') = √[ v(N+v+D−2) / (N(2v+D−2)) ] · r(vαL; v−1 α'L'),
    52	
    53	  c(N vαL; N−1, v+1, α'L') = (−1)^{L+L'} √[ (N−v)(v+D−2) / (N(2v+D−2)) ]
    54	          · √[ dim_v (2L'+1) / (dim_{v+1}(2L+1)) ] · r(v+1 α'L'; vαL),
    55	
    56	where dim_v = (2v+D−2)(v+D−3)!/(v!(D−2)!) is the dimension of the O(D) irrep (v).
    57	
    58	*Proof.* (i) P(P†)^n h = 4n(v + D/2 + n − 1)(P†)^{n−1}h for harmonic h of degree v (induction
    59	on n with [P,P†] = 4N̂+2D). Hence ‖(P†)^n h‖² = c_{n,v}‖h‖², c_{n,v} = Π_{k=1}^{n} 4k(v+D/2+k−1).
